-- title:
--   Uniform bound for twisted orbital and weighted orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $K\subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, $\nu_{Z_L}$ a Haar measure on the unit group of the adele ring of $L$, $D$ an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28) datum for $\mathcal{O}_L$ over $K\subseteq L$ (a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to ring automorphisms of the adeles of $L$, compatible with $L$ and continuous), and $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$. Fix finite sets $S_L$ of finite places of $L$ and $S$ of finite places of $K$, an archimedean factor $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$, and semi-local factors $\varphi_S(v)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$. Let $H$ be a closed subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $L$ consisting exactly of those $h$ with vanishing off-diagonal entries and with $\sigma_D(h)h^{-1}$ central, where $\sigma_D$ is the automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ induced by $D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma$, and let $\mu_H$ be a right-invariant Haar measure on $H$. Let $\Delta\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ consist of diagonal $t$ with $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11})\neq 1$, such that distinct $t,t'\in\Delta$ have disjoint $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy classes modulo the centre, i.e. disjoint sets $\{\delta : \exists g,\ t^{-1}g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g)\in Z(\mathrm{GL}_2(L))\}$. The assertion is: for every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ with $|T|\ge 2$ and with no place of $L$ above a member of $T$ lying in $S_L$, every choice, for each $v$, of an extension $w_v$ of $v$ to $L$ and of a place $w'_v$ of $L$ with $(w'_v)$ the ideal $\sigma\cdot w_v$ for $v\in T$, every family $\varpi_v$ in the valuation ring of $L_{w_v}$ with $\varpi_v$ irreducible and of nonzero image in $L_{w_v}$ for $v\in T$, all $n_v\in\mathbb{N}$ and families $r_{T,v}:\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ which for $v\in T$ form a Hecke coset system (representatives of the left cosets inside the double coset) for the integral subgroup $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathcal{O}_{w_v})$ and the element $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$, and all $z_v\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ with $z_v=\varpi_v\cdot 1$ for $v\in T$, there exists $C\ge 0$ such that the following holds for all exponent families $k,j$, all $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $L$ and $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles admitting the semi-local factorisation `IsSemiLocalFactorization` at $S\cup T$ with factors $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and, at $v$, the function $x\mapsto\sum_{\iota:\mathrm{Fin}(k_v)\to\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)}\mathbf{1}_{\text{integral set}}\bigl(\mathrm{sLC}_v(\mathrm{loc}_{w_v}(\prod_m r_{T,v}(\iota_m)\cdot z_v^{j_v}))^{-1}x\bigr)$ for $v\in T$ and $\varphi_S(v)$ otherwise (so: $\varphi_a$ is a compactly supported smooth archimedean factor, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, each factor at $v\in S\cup T$ is locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f$ is the product of the factors on elements integral outside $S\cup T$ and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi$ is the product of $\varphi_a$ on the archimedean part with $\varphi_f$ on the finite part), and all finite $\Delta_\varphi\subseteq\Delta$: writing $q$ for a chosen representative of a class in the orbit quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles by $H$, equipped with the quotient measure built from the adelic Haar measure, $H$ and $\mu_H$, and $Z_t(q)=\int^{\sim}\|\varphi(q^{-1}\,t\,\sigma_D(z\cdot 1\cdot q))\|\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)$ as a $[0,\infty]$-valued integral, one has $$\sum_{t\in\Delta_\varphi}\Bigl(\int Z_t(q)\,dq+\int\bigl|-\log\mathrm{ht}(q)-\log\mathrm{ht}(w\,q)\bigr|\,Z_t(q)\,dq\Bigr)\ \le\ C\prod_{v\in T}\bigl(N(w'_v)+1\bigr)^{k_v},$$ all integrals being $[0,\infty]$-valued Lebesgue integrals, $\mathrm{ht}$ the adelic height on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $L$, $w$ the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of the antidiagonal matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$, and $N$ the absolute norm of the underlying prime ideal.
--
--   This is the archimedean-and-finite bound for the geometric side of the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension: the unsigned orbital integrals and the height-weighted orbital integrals attached to the hyperbolic $\sigma$-twisted classes in $\Delta$, for a test function whose local components at the auxiliary places $T$ are Hecke words of length $k_v$ times a central shift, are bounded by a constant times $\prod_{v\in T}(N w'_v+1)^{k_v}$, the number of unit cosets occurring in the word, uniformly in the exponents and in the finite subset of classes. Phrasing everything with $[0,\infty]$-valued integrals makes the bound monotone in $|\varphi|$ and free of integrability side conditions; it feeds the corresponding statement for genuine (complex-valued) orbital integrals, [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_integral_norm_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_le_of_isSemiLocalFactorization`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_integral_norm_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_le_of_isSemiLocalFactorization), and the count $n_v=N w_v+1$ enters through [`NumberField.eq_absNorm_add_one_of_isHeckeCosetSystem_diagPi`](thm.html#NumberField.eq_absNorm_add_one_of_isHeckeCosetSystem_diagPi).
